; Verify the ORR+EOR macro-fusion enabled by FeatureFuseOrrEor on hip12.
;
; The NOFUSION RUN line disables only fuse-orr-eor. There is deliberately no
; function-level "target-features" attribute on these functions: a hardcoded
; target-features attribute would override -mattr and make the negative RUN
; line indistinguishable from the positive one, defeating the validation.
;
; The FUSION-ONLY RUN line uses -mcpu=generic +fuse-orr-eor so that fuse-orr-eor
; is the sole fusion feature. This guards against hasFuseOrrEor() being omitted
; from AArch64Subtarget::hasFusion(), which would silently prevent the macro
; fusion mutation from being registered when no other fuse-* feature is on.

; Positive case 1: 128-bit Q register path (ORRv16i8 / EORv16i8).
; The ORR and EOR share the same destination register, so the scheduler must
; place them adjacent when fusion is enabled.
define <4 x i32> @orr_eor_v16i8(<4 x i32> %a, <4 x i32> %b, <4 x i32> %mask, <4 x i32> %c, <4 x i32> %d, <4 x i32> %e) {
